course: dictionary
lesson: 5886
title: Good manners and meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «manners» is usually used in the plural, with an s. Manners are the polite ways of behaving with other people, like saying please and thank you. Read the words around it to find the meaning: «Good table manners as a guest make people happy to have you back.»
explain: The clues in the sentence show you the meaning. «At New Year Lín's aunties hand out hóngbāo ... and every child in the room suddenly remembers their manners.» The children remember to be polite, so manners means polite behaviour.
explain: Be careful with the singular, manner. A manner is the way a person behaves or speaks, like a friendly manner. "In a manner" means in a way. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word: "good table manners" becomes "good polite ways to eat at a table." Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Manners are the polite ways of behaving with other people.
fact: Table manners are the polite ways to eat at a table.
fact: «Manners» is usually plural. The singular «manner» means a way of doing something.
fact: «Good manners» help people feel comfortable and respected.
fact: Manners can differ between countries and families, so each home may have its own customs.
exercise: «Good table manners as a guest make people happy to have you back.» What are table manners? | Loud shouting during a meal | Ways to set up a table with forks and plates | * The polite ways to eat at a table | Rules for playing card games
exercise: «Honesty and good manners show respect.» What do good manners show? | Hunger | Sleepiness | * Respect | Anger
exercise: «At New Year every child in the room suddenly remembers their manners.» What does remembers their manners mean? | They remember where the money is | They start singing loudly | They forget their names | * They remember to behave politely
test: «Kipling's Stone Age name Taffimai Metallumai means Small-person-without-any-manners.» What does without any manners suggest? | * Rude, with no polite behaviour | Very quiet and shy | Very tidy and clean | Very tall and strong
test: Which phrase means "in a way"? | Good manners | Mind your manners | * In a manner | Table manners
exam: Which sentence uses manners to mean polite behaviour? | «He walked in a slow manner.» | «The manner of the cake was sweet.» | * «Saying please is part of good manners.» | «Her friendly manner made everyone smile.»
